module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.authored_fixtures_prove_the_core_while_the_host_feed_is_empty

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data authored_fixtures_prove_the_core_while_the_host_feed_is_empty: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "authored_fixtures_prove_the_core_while_the_host_feed_is_empty" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a lens splits into a pure core over a projection type and a thin host boundary that fills it, the core is proven by authored fixtures, and NOTHING executes the boundary -- so a feed that yields ZERO rows leaves every refusing arm unreachable and the lens permanently green** (INVALID STATE: the fixture suite constructs the projection rows DIRECTLY, which is the whole point of the split and is what makes the core witnessable; but constructing them directly is also exactly what bypasses the one function that touches the corpus. Green fixtures therefore establish that the core would refuse IF FED, and say nothing about whether it is ever fed. HARM: the lens is enrolled, reads clean on every subject forever, and is cited as coverage for a class it has never once been able to see -- DESIGN section 4b, a check whose RED is not authorable is worse than absent.)",

    "SPECIMEN AND INSTRUMENT, 2026-09-13, found by running the boundary rather than by reading it. `gunbc.authored_position_field_lens` was written to answer whether a row type authors a position (`ordinal`, `index`, `position`) that a declared `List` of that type ALREADY fixes -- the class review 65389, review 65422 and review 65456 each found separately inside gunbc#11181. Its nine authored witness arms passed, including a discriminating RED that refused a listed row type and two controls that admitted an unlisted one. The host feed was then probed directly against the live corpus: `v2.std.decl_index` `data_decl_type_facts` returns 20863 declarations and `element_type_of_declared_type` matched ZERO of them, because `DataDeclTypeFact.type_name` renders a generic as its BARE HEAD -- `data authored_position_field_names: List<String>` reads back as the four characters `List`, with the argument dropped. The second half of the question was therefore undecidable on every real subject, the refusing arm was unreachable, and the nine green arms could not have detected it.",

    "THE SECOND AUTHORITY WAS PROBED TOO, so this is a capability gap rather than a wrong feed choice. The `DataItem` arm of `v2.std.decl_index` `decl_facts` carries the initializer projection, and an initializer of list elements would name its element constructors; `v2.std.fn_index` `callee_texts_in_subtree` over that node returned EMPTY for the data declarations probed. No corpus surface available today carries the element type of a declared generic, which is why the lens was NOT landed in a permanently-green state and the class was recorded instead.",

    "THE RECOGNITION RULE, stated so it is checkable without re-deriving the specimen: a lens carries this class when its fixtures construct the projection type directly AND no enrolled evidence asserts that the host boundary returns a NON-EMPTY population on a subject known to inhabit the class. The tell is structural and cheap -- a projection type whose only constructors in the repository are inside the test module. The repair is also cheap and is NOT another fixture: probe the boundary once against a real subject and assert a positive control, or give the feed its own refusing arm so an empty population reads as UNREAD rather than as CLEAN, the way `gunbc.bare_name_fork_lens` already does for an unread SUBJECT and neither it nor this lens did for the FEED.",

    "THE RUNG, with its ceiling. Found at MITIGATABLE: the split is a good shape and the gap is caught only by someone choosing to run the boundary, which is a discipline and not a mechanism. The ceiling is MECHANICALLY PREVENTABLE and it is reachable without new language capability: a projection type whose constructors appear only under a test module is derivable from the same `Node` tree the namespace authority already walks, so a lens over lenses can refuse the shape. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, named as a capability rather than as an artifact: constructor-site facts for a declared type, partitioned by whether the site is inside the witness layer, sufficient to decide for EVERY projection type whether any non-test site constructs it. A separate and independent trigger retires the specimen rather than the class: element-type facts for a declared generic, at which point `authored_position_field_lens` becomes decidable and can land with a real positive control.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
